{title: Upon The Cross Extended}
{artist: Paul Gerhardt · tr. John Kelly}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
Upon the cross extended, See, world, thy Lord suspended,
Thy Savior yields His breath. The Prince of Life from heaven
Himself hath freely given To shame and blows and bitter death.

Verse 2
Come hither now and ponder, 'Twill fill thy soul with wonder,
Blood streams from every pore. Through grief whose depth none knoweth,
From His great heart there floweth Sigh after sigh of anguish o'er.

Verse 3
Who is it that hath bruised Thee? Who hath so sore abused Thee
And caused Thee all Thy woe? While we must make confession
Of sin and dire transgression, Thou deeds of evil dost not know.

Verse 4
I caused Thy grief and sighing By evils multiplying
As countless as the sands. I caused the woes unnumbered
With which Thy soul is cumbered, Thy sorrows raised by wicked hands.

Verse 5
'Tis I who should be smitten My doom should here be written:
Bound hand and foot in hell. The fetters and the scourging,
The floods around Thee surging, 'Tis I who have deserved them well.
